<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> The Holy Spirit is the third Person of the Trinity, who dwells in us, sanctifies us, and leads us to Christ.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that the Holy Spirit is a divine Person, not a force or energy.</li>
<li>Know the names, symbols, and mission of the Holy Spirit.</li>
<li>Recognize the Spirit's action in the life of Christ, of Mary, and of the Church.</li>
<li>Learn the gifts and fruits of the Holy Spirit.</li>
<li>Live a personal relationship with the Holy Spirit who dwells in the heart.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;The Spirit helps us in our weakness, for we do not know how to pray as we ought, but the Spirit himself intercedes for us with groanings too deep for words&raquo; (Rom 8:26)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 683-747</p>

</section>

